          "text": "Yes. Structured prompting principles transfer across major language models including ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, and Microsoft Copilot. Exact response behavior may vary slightly by model version, but the Role + Context + Task + Format + Constraint input formula remains consistent and effective across all major platforms."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How many prompts should I test before finalizing one?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Standard practice recommends testing 3 to 5 variations per task to identify the highest-performing structure. Once identified, that structure becomes a reusable template in your AI content workflow. Iterating with feedback — such as appending 'What is missing from this output?' or 'Improve the [specific section] above' — refines results within the same session without starting over."
        }
      },
