        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is an AI prompt?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "An AI prompt is a written instruction given to an AI model that defines the task, context, format, and constraints. It functions as a task brief — the model reads it, interprets the intent, and generates output based only on the information provided. The quality of that instruction directly determines the quality of the output. Most users get poor results not because the AI tool is limited, but because the prompt lacks the information the model needs to perform the task correctly."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How do I improve AI prompt results?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Add a role, specify the audience, define output format, and include constraints. The more specific the input, the more accurate and usable the output. Use the ROLE + TASK + AUDIENCE + FORMAT + CONSTRAINT formula. The second you tell the AI who it is, who the output is for, how long the output should be, and what to avoid — editing time drops from 30–60 minutes to under 10 minutes per output."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is prompt engineering?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Prompt engineering techniques are structured methods for writing AI instructions that consistently produce accurate, targeted outputs. It includes role assignment, format control, constraint definition, few-shot prompting, chain-of-thought prompting, and iteration. It is a communication skill applied to AI tools — not a programming or technical skill — and it is now a listed job requirement across content, marketing, HR, legal, and data roles."
        }
      },
