        "name": "What are the 8 core LLM prompt engineering techniques?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "The 8 core LLM prompt engineering techniques are: 1) Role Assignment — assigning a specific expert identity to the AI before the task; 2) Chain-of-Thought Prompting — instructing the AI to reason step by step before providing the final answer; 3) Few-Shot Prompting — providing 2–3 examples of desired output before asking for a new one; 4) Output Format Instructions — specifying exactly how the response should be structured; 5) Constraint Setting — defining what the AI should NOT do to force precision; 6) Persona and Audience Targeting — combining the AI's assigned role with a defined target audience; 7) Iterative Prompting — following up on initial outputs with refinement instructions in a multi-step AI content workflow; and 8) Negative Instructions — explicitly listing what the output should exclude such as specific words, phrases, or formats."
