          "text": "Chain of thought prompting is a prompt engineering technique that instructs a large language model to generate intermediate reasoning steps before producing a final answer. It was formally introduced in the 2022 Google Research paper 'Chain-of-Thought Prompting Elicits Reasoning in Large Language Models' by Wei et al. The study showed GPT-3 achieved 58% accuracy on the GSM8K math benchmark with chain of thought prompting, compared to 17% with standard prompting — a 3.4x improvement. Stanford University research has confirmed that step-by-step decomposition reduces hallucination rates, and McKinsey (2023) found structured reasoning frameworks reduce human post-editing by up to 40%."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What are the 8 professional use cases for chain of thought prompting?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "The 8 professional use cases for chain of thought prompting are: 1) Mathematical and logical reasoning — outperforming standard prompts on math benchmarks by 20 to 50%; 2) Multi-step content creation — separating outline, drafting, and editing into sequential steps for higher consistency; 3) Code generation and debugging — instructing the model to first interpret code, identify the issue, then output a correction; 4) Market and competitor research — breaking prompts into audience identification, pain points, competitive landscape, and messaging recommendation; 5) Academic summarization — producing up to 37% improvement in source relevance scores over single-query approaches; 6) Email and proposal drafting — defining objective, audience, and tone as discrete steps before requesting a draft; 7) Decision analysis — prompting the AI to list pros, cons, constraints, and a recommendation in sequence; and 8) Workflow automation planning — mapping multi-tool process dependencies before generating a final workflow or checklist."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What are the 5 steps for writing an effective chain of thought prompt?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "The 5 steps for writing an effective chain of thought prompt are: Step 1 — Define the role and context first by specifying the AI's task scope, subject domain, and any constraints before issuing instructions. Step 2 — Decompose the task into ordered steps using explicit sequencing language such as 'First… Then… Next… Finally…' to establish the reasoning chain. Step 3 — Request reasoning before the final output by including an instruction such as 'Explain your reasoning at each step before providing the final answer.' Step 4 — Specify output format by defining the required structure — bullet list, table, numbered steps, or paragraph — to prevent format variability across runs. Step 5 — Iterate and standardize by testing the prompt across multiple inputs, refining for consistency, and storing successful versions as reusable templates in your AI content workflow library."
        }
      }
    ]
